{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1340626-which-came-first-pyros-divine-fire-or-the-god-machine","id":1340626,"title":"Which came first? Pyros (Divine Fire) or the God-Machine?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-10T08:49:19-07:00","id":1340626,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Which came first? Pyros (Divine Fire) or the God-Machine?","content":"I have an on-going debate in my CoD gaming group on which came first. The Divine Fire or the God-Machine?<br /> <br /> The story of &quot;Giants in the Earth&quot; gives an alternate creation.<br /> <br /> Anyone care to wade in? What do your chronicles have as the &quot;creation&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14512-ghostdriver","name":"Ghostdriver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14512_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T10:26:08-07:00","id":1340641,"title":"","content":"Well to me it seems like the divine flame came first, while the god machine was soon developed later in the universe in order to manage and maintain it. just as natural life came before machines so too would the god machine come after Pyros","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24642-mr-perfect-cell","name":"Mr.Perfect cell","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T11:33:14-07:00","id":1340650,"title":"","content":"The short answer is: Whichever one you want in first.<br /> <br /> A longer answer is complicated because the timeline of deities coming into being is inherently mysterious and also largely unimportant for most games, and the God-machine has a nasty habit of retroactively inserting itself into points at time in such a way as to have always been first if it wants to, and trying to nail which came first also comes from how you think of each of them and what causes what, which can even be in a retroactive sense.<br /> <br /> BUT, I can say this since I once spent an inordinate amount of time working out a lot of Chronicles stuff to get a rough chronology of this sort of thing, and in most cases, the most likely part of the established cosmology to have come first would be Mummy's cosmology/mythology/history.<br /> <br /> Now, what do I have as creation in my games? Usually nothing, because I'm very much interested in games where that sort of stuff is unimportant, and leaving it unanswered can help the feeling of wonder and horror as much as it does in real life-but if I have to answer that question when I don't have a chronicle-specific answer for it, then the answer is &quot;In the beginning, Arcane and his friends sat down to play a roleplaying game.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T11:36:45-07:00","id":1340653,"title":"","content":"Not sure, but I think they're opposites. The Principle and the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T12:10:01-07:00","id":1340656,"title":"","content":"Maybe not Opposites, but the Yin to the Others Yang Both Necessary for existence. <br /> <br /> Maybe they where once A Singular Being, before being split up like Meow Wolf? <a href=\"https://meowwolf.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://meowwolf.com/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T12:22:18-07:00","id":1340661,"title":"","content":"Hmmm. Interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T12:32:02-07:00","id":1340662,"title":"","content":"I always believed the God-Machine and The Principle were two sides of the same being. A cosmic level entity that works on both maintaining the status quo and pushing it to change. Both are necessary for life to exist, and I'm not sure why I initially started believing it, but I just can't untangle the two in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25226-knightfenrirwulfhart","name":"KnightFenrirWulfhart","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-10T12:53:47-07:00","id":1340664,"title":"","content":"By contrast, I've never had any association between the two of them. Personal boredom with the ease of connection asides, I found that the coincidence of the parallels and comparisons to be both more in line with the setting in general* and satisfying for my own takes on it than any actual connection between the two, particularly for those moments where I bother nodding in cosmic horror's direction.<br /> <br /> People favor conspiracy over absence for a reason, and I like to exploit that reason in a lot of my stories and games.<br /> <br /> *which is not to say there's no precedence for the connection within the canon, both in directly talking about the possible connections between the two and contrasting it with the Seers and Angels playing in the same ballparks with each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-10-2019, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}